{
  "manufacturer": "Lochinvar",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lochinvar",
  "model": "Copper-fin II / IIE boiler, water heater and pool heater (ModBus communication board)",
  "model_slug": "copper-fin-ii-iie-modbus",
  "short_model": "Copper-fin II/IIE",
  "aliases": [
    "Copper-fin II",
    "Copper-fin IIE",
    "CBX",
    "CFX",
    "CHX",
    "CPX",
    "C(F,H,P)X",
    "Copperfin"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler",
  "applies_to": "Lochinvar Copper-fin II/IIE boilers and water heaters 402-2072 and pool heaters 502-2072 with the MTR-01 ModBus board, per manual 100160882 Rev G.",
  "summary": "Copper-fin II and IIE copper-tube boilers, water heaters and pool heaters talk Modbus RTU through Lochinvar's MTR-01 communication board on RS-485. The map uses coils for stage and tank-thermostat enables, discrete inputs for safety switches and outputs, input registers for temperatures, firing rate and status/blocking/lockout codes, and holding registers for configuration bits and BAS-supplied temperatures. All values are 16-bit; temperatures are degrees C x 10.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Addresses are printed Modicon-style (00001 coils, 10001 discrete inputs, 30001 input registers, 40001 holding registers). Subtract the table base and 1 for the wire address; the exception-code text describes PDU addresses starting at 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Copper-fin II/IIE Boiler, Water Heater and Pool Heater - ModBus and BACnet Communication Instructions",
    "doc_number": "100160882_2000001229 Rev G",
    "revision_date": "2026-01",
    "url": "https://assets.lochinvar.com/damroot/Original/10017/C(F,H,P)X-MODB_100160882_2000001229_REV%20G_(69837).pdf",
    "pages": "ModBus configuration p. 4; functions and exceptions pp. 5-6; memory map pp. 7-8; unit operation pp. 20-23; conversions p. 23; status/blocking codes p. 24; lockout codes p. 25"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Temperatures: the conversion section says temperatures pass in degrees C with the decimal value divided by 10 (worked examples: 26.7 C sent as 267, 683 read as 68.3 C), so scale 0.1 is used.",
    "Left out: System/Cascade set point (30004), Outlet set point (30008) and Pool set point (40004). The map prints a 0.5 resolution for these while the conversion section says temperature data is C x 10, so their scaling is not settled.",
    "Registers with a negative published minimum (inlet, pool, tank, outdoor, supply/return temperatures) are typed INT16; the manual only says 16-bit word. Outlet temperature is also typed INT16 for consistency with the other temperatures.",
    "Status codes are also listed for input register 30023 and blocking codes for 30024 in the troubleshooting section, but those registers are not in the memory map, so they are not listed.",
    "The lockout code list is in the manual (p. 25); 30016 changes during operation and should be read only when the status code is 40.",
    "The BACnet section says dip switch 8 selects C or F; in the ModBus section switch 8 is an address bit (value 128). Units here assume C, as in the conversion examples."
  ],
